+ * (0x10700000, Linux's clk-exynos990.c: the gates it names, six to a line). The CMUs and the pin
+ * controllers are always readable; the I2C block is read last, a line on the screen before each of its registers
+ * (a gated block that never answers stops the phone there: force restart).
